### AutoParts ERP - sample requests
### Install the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client) and click "Send Request" above any block.

@host = https://localhost:7150
@tenant = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### Service info: which modules are loaded
GET {{host}}/

### Health
GET {{host}}/health

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reference data
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Brands, with a count of the parts carrying each
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/brands
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

### Categories
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/categories
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

### Create a brand
POST {{host}}/api/catalog/brands
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

{
  "code": "TRW",
  "name": "TRW Automotive",
  "isOriginalEquipment": false,
  "countryCode": "DE"
}

### Create a category
POST {{host}}/api/catalog/categories
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

{
  "code": "BRK-DSC",
  "name": "Brake Discs",
  "sortOrder": 20
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The searches the business actually runs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Everything recorded as fitting a 2015 Golf VII
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/parts/for-vehicle?make=Volkswagen&model=Golf VII&year=2015
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

### Narrowed by engine code - far fewer wrong-fit returns
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/parts/for-vehicle?make=Volkswagen&model=Golf VII&year=2015&engineCode=CJZA
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

### An OEM number read off the old part, typed with spaces
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/parts?term=5Q0 698 151 A
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

### The same number without them. Same result - that is the point.
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/parts?term=5q0698151a
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

### A few words from the description
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/parts?term=brake pad
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

### Only parts sold against a returnable core
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/parts?requiresCoreReturn=true
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

### One part by SKU, the way a counter terminal looks it up
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/parts/by-sku/BP-1188
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Setting up a new part
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1. Create it. Copy a brandId and categoryId from the list calls above.
# @name createPart
POST {{host}}/api/catalog/parts
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

{
  "sku": "BD-3301",
  "manufacturerPartNumber": "DF 4249",
  "brandId": "REPLACE-WITH-A-BRAND-ID",
  "categoryId": "REPLACE-WITH-A-CATEGORY-ID",
  "name": "Brake disc, front axle, vented",
  "stockUnitCode": "EA",
  "description": "Vented front brake disc, 312mm."
}

@partId = {{createPart.response.body.$}}

### 2. Link the OEM number a customer will quote
POST {{host}}/api/catalog/parts/{{partId}}/cross-references
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

{
  "kind": "Oem",
  "number": "5Q0 615 301 F",
  "sourceBrand": "VW",
  "notes": "312mm vented"
}

### 3. Record what it fits
POST {{host}}/api/catalog/parts/{{partId}}/fitments
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

{
  "make": "Volkswagen",
  "model": "Golf VII",
  "yearFrom": 2012,
  "yearTo": 2020,
  "engineCode": "CJZA",
  "position": "FRONT"
}

### 4. Make it orderable and sellable
POST {{host}}/api/catalog/parts/{{partId}}/activate
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

### 5. Read it back in full
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/parts/{{partId}}
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rules the API will refuse - each returns a stable errorCode
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Duplicate SKU -> 409 catalog.part.sku_exists
POST {{host}}/api/catalog/parts
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

{
  "sku": "BP-1188",
  "manufacturerPartNumber": "99 999 99",
  "brandId": "REPLACE-WITH-A-BRAND-ID",
  "categoryId": "REPLACE-WITH-A-CATEGORY-ID",
  "name": "Duplicate SKU test",
  "stockUnitCode": "EA"
}

### Activating an already-discontinued part -> 422 catalog.part.cannot_reactivate
POST {{host}}/api/catalog/parts/{{partId}}/discontinue
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

{}

### Missing required fields -> 400 with every bad field listed at once
POST {{host}}/api/catalog/parts
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

{
  "sku": "",
  "manufacturerPartNumber": "",
  "brandId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "categoryId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "name": "",
  "stockUnitCode": "PARSEC"
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Purchasing
#
# The full loop, in order. Steps 1-2 need a supplier and a part you already
# have: grab them from /api/partners?isSupplier=true and /api/catalog/parts.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1. Start a draft order. The order number is assigned server-side.
POST {{host}}/api/purchasing/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

{
  "supplierId": "REPLACE-WITH-A-SUPPLIER-PARTNER-ID",
  "supplierCode": "BOSCH",
  "warehouseId": "REPLACE-WITH-A-WAREHOUSE-ID",
  "currencyCode": "EUR",
  "notes": "Weekly stock order."
}

### 2. Put a part on it. Sku and description are snapshotted onto the document.
POST {{host}}/api/purchasing/orders/{{orderId}}/lines
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

{
  "partId": "REPLACE-WITH-A-PART-ID",
  "sku": "BP-1188",
  "description": "Brake pad set, front",
  "quantity": 10,
  "unitCode": "EA",
  "unitPrice": 24.50
}

### 3. Send it to the supplier. This is the point of commitment.
POST {{host}}/api/purchasing/orders/{{orderId}}/submit
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

{ "expectedOn": "2026-09-15" }

### 4. Record their acknowledgement.
POST {{host}}/api/purchasing/orders/{{orderId}}/confirm
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

{ "expectedOn": "2026-09-16", "supplierReference": "ACK-77213" }

### 5. Book part of the delivery in. Inventory picks this up and adds the stock.
POST {{host}}/api/purchasing/orders/{{orderId}}/lines/{{lineId}}/receipts
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

{ "quantity": 6 }

### 6. Check the stock actually moved - on hand should have gone up by 6.
GET {{host}}/api/inventory/stock?partId={{partId}}
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

### The order now reads PartiallyReceived, with 4 still outstanding
GET {{host}}/api/purchasing/orders/{{orderId}}
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

### The buyer's working list
GET {{host}}/api/purchasing/orders?outstandingOnly=true
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

### Orders past their promised date
GET {{host}}/api/purchasing/orders?overdueOnly=true
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

### Look one up the way you read it off a delivery note
GET {{host}}/api/purchasing/orders/by-number/PO-2026-00001
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Replenishment
#
# Nothing creates these by hand. Issue stock in Inventory until a part drops
# below its reorder point and one appears here on its own.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Parts that have run low, worst shortfall first
GET {{host}}/api/purchasing/suggestions
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

### Roll one onto a draft order and mark it dealt with
POST {{host}}/api/purchasing/suggestions/{{suggestionId}}/order-line
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

{
  "purchaseOrderId": "REPLACE-WITH-A-DRAFT-ORDER-ID",
  "sku": "BP-1188",
  "description": "Brake pad set, front",
  "unitCode": "EA",
  "unitPrice": 24.50
}

### Or decide not to buy it, with a reason
POST {{host}}/api/purchasing/suggestions/{{suggestionId}}/dismiss
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

{ "reason": "Being run down; sell the shelf stock first." }

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rules Purchasing will refuse
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Receiving more than was ordered -> 422 purchasing.line.over_receipt
POST {{host}}/api/purchasing/orders/{{orderId}}/lines/{{lineId}}/receipts
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

{ "quantity": 9999 }

### Editing an order that has gone out -> 422 purchasing.order.not_editable
DELETE {{host}}/api/purchasing/orders/{{orderId}}/lines/{{lineId}}
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

### Cancelling after goods arrived -> 422 purchasing.order.cannot_cancel_after_receipt
POST {{host}}/api/purchasing/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

{ "reason": "Changed our mind." }

### Accepting the shortfall instead -> 204
POST {{host}}/api/purchasing/orders/{{orderId}}/close-short
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenant}}

{ "reason": "Supplier had no more; agreed to leave it." }
